WHY THIS EXISTS RATHER THAN A REAL SRD
--------------------------------------

The test-infrastructure spec calls for an open-licensed SRD, and defers which
one: the constraint is licence plus enough rules, lore, tables, and statblocks to
exercise every route. Emberlight is a stand-in that satisfies the second half
completely and the first half by construction, since the project owns it.

It is deliberately small and deliberately complete. Every shape the pack format
distinguishes appears at least once:

  - verbatim-class rules, with a rollable table nested inside one of them
  - a non-verbatim setting chunk with a rollable table nested inside it, which is
    the case redaction exists for
  - statblocks, read-aloud text, and glossary entries
  - a second book, so cross-source behaviour is exercised rather than assumed
  - a builder-written derived summary carrying claim-scoped citations
  - an erratum targeting a book the pack does not contain, so the inert case is
    covered
  - constraints in four of the five predicate forms
  - aliases that do not appear in the text at all, so the query rewrite has
    something real to do

Swapping in a genuine SRD is a change to this directory and nothing else. The
builder reads the JSON beside this file; it has no knowledge of Emberlight.
